    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Change the default WordPress login URL using a custom slug and (optionally) hide wp-login.php and /wp-admin/ for guests (404 response).<br />\nIncludes a visual login page designer in Settings.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin ZIP and activate it.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Login URL &amp; Designer.</li>\n<li>Set your custom login slug and options.</li>\n<li>Re-save Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Permalinks to ensure rewrite rules are active.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.5.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Use reachable Plugin URI.</li>\n<li>Fix: Avoid reading user input in public routes (nonce warnings).</li>\n<li>Fix: Escape inline CSS with wp_kses and sanitize custom CSS.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Dotsquares Custom Login URL &amp; Page Designer lets you change the login URL and customize the login page style from the admin.",
    "description": "<p>Change the default WordPress login URL using a custom slug and (optionally) hide wp-login.php and /wp-admin/ for guests (404 response).<br />\nIncludes a visual login page designer in Settings.</p>\n",
